  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only consumer must delegate load/store using node_path\n without resolving contents. Domain requires the callback, but invoking\n this guard would violate the no-content-read invariant of the test.\n Other graph fixtures exercise content resolution."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is a valid coverage-exception proposal.\n\n- **Form:** It is a fenced citation with commentary on an explicit function that has a body. That is the form `habeas:coverage` allows. The exception covers only this function's zero execution, not the file's threshold.\n- **Reason:** The commentary gives a substantive reason, not just difficulty. `StoredGraph` is a storage-only fixture. `Domain` requires `node_content`, as the `trait[Domain]/fn[node_content]` declaration in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs` shows. The fixture's tests only delegate load and store through `node_path`, and the function body is a deliberate `panic!` guard against content reads. If the guard ran, the no-content-read invariant would be broken, so zero execution is correct.\n- **Agreement with source:** The tests that use `StoredGraph` call only `load_evidence`, `store_evidence` and `verify`. The `verify` call uses `StoredReview`, whose `execute` reads no nodes, so the record it stores has no `Dependency::Node` entries. Content reads do occur in `graph.rs` (`prepare_read` and `dependencies_are_current`). `dependencies_are_current` calls `node_content` only for `Dependency::Node` entries, and the fixture's records contain none. So the guard is not reached.\n- **Other fixtures:** The claim that other fixtures exercise content resolution holds. The `Memory` domain's `impl[Memory/Domain]/fn[node_content]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` does real content resolution.\n- **No redundancy:** The item carries no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same target, so the citation is not redundant.",
